# Where project/gate/old-words.sh lets an old word through. One entry per line, fields separated by tabs: a path
# glob (`*` within a directory, `**` across), optionally a regular expression (any case) that a line must match
# to pass, and always the reason, starting with #. A glob without a pattern allows the whole file.

# The rename's own record and history, kept as written.
project/archive/**		# written in the earlier vocabulary, each with a header saying so
project/plans/exam-variant-attempt.md		# the plan names the old words it replaces
project/plans/exam-variant-attempt-removal.md		# the work-list names the old words it removes
CHANGELOG.md		# released entries keep the words of their time; the rename's entry carries the name map
project/gate/**		# the gate names the words it looks for

# The user's, pending: not reworded in step 1.
project/todo.md		# loose ends; each section needs a person's judgement
project/plans/agent-neutral-runs.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/jev-judge-research.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/jev-trial.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/onboarding.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/lab.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/lab-report-worked-example.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/oracle-in-proctor.md		# open plan, the user's to reword or archive
project/plans/setup/**		# the setup wizard's plan and screen mockups; not on the work-list, the user's to reword or archive

# Not proctor's model, or frozen output of an earlier version.
project/learnings/**		# notes on other tools and dated findings, kept as written (the work-list keeps them)
project/lab/**		# throwaway trials over the frozen datasets, which keep the old layout
bench/**		# the judge bench: its own proctor root at an earlier version, unrelated to the rename
docs/reports/**		# published reports, rendered by an earlier version
Proctor.Tests/fixtures/**		# captured transcripts and trajectories, as the agents wrote them

# The one place an old word is the point.
**	\bno resume verb\b	# D15: after a crash a person or an agent looks for "resume", so the CLI help, docs/cli.md, the skill and exam-authoring say there is none

# Ordinary English or another tool's word.
**	\btest suites?\b	# a project's own tests
**	\btable cells?\b	# a cell of a table
project/plans/on-disk-layout.md	evaluation suite	# the literature's word for an exam, in the words table
